{"availability":"available","full":"orassayag/project-cosmos","name":"project-cosmos","description":"A living map of your architecture: services are stars, Kafka topics orbit between them, and real flows play as comets with payloads. Ask questions to a LangGraph AI agent; a nightly Drift Sync agent opens one PR per team when code drifts. Incident replay, blast radius, health, ownership views. Mobile-first. React, TypeScript, Vite, SVG maps.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-30T14:35:34Z","updated":"2026-10-08T21:20:56Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://project-cosmos-six.vercel.app","topics":["ai-agent","animation","architecture","architecture-diagram","developer-tools","documentation","event-driven","incident-management","kafka","langchain","langgraph","llm","microservices","observability","react","svg","system-design","typescript","visualization","vite"],"demo":"https://project-cosmos-six.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.864Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.864Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.864Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T23:43:11.864Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Every service is a star. Kafka topics orbit between them. Real flows play as comets you can watch, pause, and inspect — payloads included. Ask the map a question in plain English and an AI agent answers from the map itself. And a nightly AI agent keeps the whole map honest against your actual code.","Originally based on Cosmos OS — see Origin & credits.","Every architecture diagram starts dying the moment it's born. The wiki page is from two reorgs ago, the Lucidchart link is stale, and the only reliable documentation is a senior engineer with a whiteboard. Project Cosmos takes a different bet:"],"features":["The server owns the map, in git; the client renders it. Everything you see — services, topics, flows — is one set of plain TypeScript files under server/src/cosmos/data/, served at GET /api/cosmos. No database, no sync…","Flows are playable, not drawn. A scenario is a real request traced hop-by-hop: URL, headers, payload, what got produced to which topic, what got written to which database. Press play and watch it fly.","Honesty is automated. A nightly agent diffs your repos against the map and opens one PR per team when reality moved. Forgetting to update the docs stops being an option.","Questions get answered from the map, not from guesses. The AI agent only knows what the map knows, and can only point at services and scenarios that really exist on it."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b9f3c75c4aa06cafe3ea77f044b8c0d73c29671fdd0d12a3ad9f3ffe50b26f64","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.041Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.041Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Every service is a star. Kafka topics orbit between them. Real flows play as comets you can watch, pause, and inspect — payloads included. Ask the map a question in plain English and an AI agent answers from the map itself. And a nightly AI agent keeps the whole map honest against your actual code.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"npm run dev starts the client (Vite, :5173) and the API server (:8787) together, no account needed; Vite forwards /api/ to the server, and the map loads its data from GET /api/cosmos.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"not_required","text":"They need the variables below; the dev server reads them from .env.local at the repo root, then server/.env (no Vercel account needed):","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"optional","text":"Full setup (GitHub PAT, Anthropic API key, optional Slack) in drift-sync/README.md.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b9f3c75c4aa06cafe3ea77f044b8c0d73c29671fdd0d12a3ad9f3ffe50b26f64","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.041Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T21:20:56Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/orassayag/project-cosmos/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T23:43:12.043Z","hash":"b9f3c75c4aa06cafe3ea77f044b8c0d73c29671fdd0d12a3ad9f3ffe50b26f64","originalBytes":33683,"storedBytes":33683,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["server","run","cosmos","map","npm","api","data","demo","src","agent","client","every","key","one","what","vercel","service","real","dev","incident","incidents","scenario","services","get","never","any","ask","drift","only","step","tours","app","claude","when","answer","jev","open","project","test","topic","visitor","architecture","domain","gateway","payments","see","topics","version","view","bash","click","cookie","copy","does","ownership","same","scripts","team","time","triage","types","which","without","answers","both","box","build","change","checkout","drift-sync","edit","everything","github","it.","mode","own","per","play","question","repo","start","sync","through","vite","whole","after","astromart","checks","commit","connect","file","health","install","langchain","langgraph","layout","live","over","panel","payloads","press","reads","scenarios","serves","shows","star","steps","tests","their","them","tour","views","add-scenario","add-service","already","back","blast","changed","clone","drag","env","first","fixture","fresh","git","kafka","keys","link","local","nightly","openai","opens","owns","page","phaseid","plain","playwright","post","provider","questions","radius","read","readme.md","record","repos","show","skills","timeout","tools"